From 635513a4740f14a9f416ea59b18fe85af56c39a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:31:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix manager guard-creation, cross-society approval hole, and
 cleanup

approve-registration refused managers with "Admin only" while the UI
offered them the Add-a-guard form and RLS accepted the insert, so the
form failed on its second step and left the request pending. It also
never checked that the request belonged to the caller's own society --
and because it runs with the service role, RLS could not catch that
either, so any admin could approve a pending request (including an
'admin' request) in someone else's society. Temp passwords were derived
from Date.now(), making them enumerable; they are now random.

The capability table in src/lib/permissions.ts had no callers. A manager
therefore saw the same Delete button an admin does, which called
delete-user and returned a bare 403 after the confirmation dialog. The
admin sidebar and UserRegistry now read it.

Also: clear all 5 eslint errors, delete the unused inactivity-logout
hook, point config.toml at the live project, and document the hand-run
schema files with a query that reports which are applied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SkgQmEqqV81BLi8paSpkvE
